The per-file corrections of a stereo file's input are the stereo layer's menu, "3D Input Format" in the context
menu (ORDER 512 and 551; Daniel, 2026-10-23: "never touch the user file"): Automatic, Not 3D, every packing in
either order, the anaglyph pairs, picture and depth, Swap left and right eyes, and Save the correction into the
file. The choice is kept in the layer's per-file store, $XDG_STATE_HOME/stereo-policy/files, which the thumbnailers,
the information panel and the viewers read too, so a wide screenshot set to Not 3D is flat everywhere. Nothing is
written into the file unless the person chooses the save.

Videos get the menu with a video's list: every packing of the frame packing SEI of H.264 and H.265, of Matroska's
StereoMode and of st3d, frames in turn and both views in one block included. A thumbnail is one frame, so those two
show one view there; their entries stay in the list and say so.

Swap Eyes (the menu and Alt+Shift+W) keeps its choice in that store and no longer writes the file attribute
user.stereo-policy.swap-eyes. An attribute an earlier version wrote is still read, and is taken out of the file when
the person next changes that file's choice.

A file's choice follows it when it is renamed or moved, here or by any other program's file job
(Stereo::FileChoiceMoves); a copy carries nothing.

A store that cannot be written, a save the file's format cannot carry and a choice that could not follow its file
are said in the view's message bar with the reason; the choice is then not shown as kept.

Built against libstereo-layer-dev 1.18.0, and the build stops with CMake's message when the layer is older
(CMAKE_REQUIRE_FIND_PACKAGE_StereoLayer): before, an older layer gave a Dolphin without stereo and no error.
